# Research Record: CLI-Anything Reference Intake

Year: 2026
Topic: cli-anything-reference

Question:
  Does the external reference HKUDS/CLI-Anything
  (https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything) contain evidence that
  would require an SDDRA knowledge/skill update?

Sources:
  - https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything — official repo README
    (L1 official repo, 49.4k stars, Apache-2.0, 885 commits,
    v0.2.0)
  - CLI-Hub registry: registry.json / public_registry.json /
    matrix_registry.json (L1 official repo)
  - arXiv 2606.03854 tech report (L2 maintainer docs)
  (no RIE tmp snapshot used; no code cloned, no web data cached
  beyond the fetched README — [R96] compliant)

Findings (evidence-backed, no raw content copied):

  1. PRIMITIVE MATCH — On-demand loading: CLI-Anything v0.2.0
     HARNESS.md progressive disclosure: detailed guides extracted
     into guides/ for on-demand loading (2026-03-30). Mirrors
     SDDRA EXPAND protocol (InitialLoad manifest, context/cache
     pull-based loading) — different mechanism, same principle.
     Evidence: README news entry, 2026-03-30.

  2. PRIMITIVE MATCH — Auto-generated skill definition: Phase 6.5
     SKILL.md generation via skill_generator.py (extracts
     metadata from Click decorators, setup.py, README), writes
     canonical repo-root skill file. Mirrors SDDRA 3-way command
     registry (R98) + skill ecosystem (/sdd-skills).
     Evidence: README 2026-03-16, line 1600.

  3. PRIMITIVE MATCH — Autonomous discovery: CLI-Hub meta-skill
     (2026-03-23) lets agents discover+install CLIs autonomously;
     distributed on ClawHub, SkillHub, SkillHub.cn via
     `npx skills add HKUDS/CLI-Anything --skill cli-hub-meta-skill`.
     Mirrors SDDRA /sdd-marketplace + .agents/plugins/marketplace.json.
     Evidence: README 2026-03-23, lines 853-855.

  4. PRIMITIVE MATCH — Evidence model: per-CLI test baselines
     (unit + E2E; real-software invocation verification; TEST.md
     with plans+results) — 2,461 tests total (1,732 unit + 579 E2E
     + 19 Node, 100% pass) across 20+ harnesses. Mirrors
     DONE-PROOF (5-dimension proof) + E2E BDD tests.
     Evidence: README badges + tests tree (gimp 107, blender 208,
     libreoffice 158, joplin 134, calibre 58, openscreen 101...).

  5. PRIMITIVE MATCH — Registry integrity: copy-before-`_source`-tagging
     hardening (2026-05-17 #281) prevents mutation of cached/mocked
     registry data. Mirrors SDDRA 3-way registry sync ([R98]) +
     INDEX routing immutability.
     Evidence: README 2026-05-17.

  6. CROSS-REF — Multi-platform distribution: CLI-Anything supports
     12 named platforms (Pi, OpenClaw, Nanobot, Cursor, Claude Code,
     OpenCode, Codex, Hermes, Reasonix, Antigravity, Qodercli,
     GitHub Copilot CLI) with per-platform install (plugin dirs).
     SDDRA has 8 plugin surfaces (.claude, .codex, .cursor, .hermes,
     .kimi, .pi, .opencode, .agents). Minor coverage gap; no spec
     change — knowledge only.
     Evidence: README platforms list (line 870).

  7. REFERENCE — Security hardening events (CLI-native): defusedxml
     for untrusted XML/SVG/ODF/MLT/CSL parse (#296, 2026-05-19);
     path-traversal+symlink escape hardening (Sketch #304,
     2026-05-21); URL validation+DOM sanitization (DomShell #156,
     2026-04-07); GIMP Script-Fu path injection fix (2026-03-14);
     guarded SQLCipher write paths + backup-required forced writes
     (Rekordbox #252, 2026-05-20); Zoom token permissions hardening.
     Adopted as L1 reference material for future CLI-runtime
     security spec — not imported as SDDRA spec change.
     Evidence: README news entries.

Decision: NO_VALUE — research does not obligate skill creation
([EVO-07]). CLI-Anything consistently MIRrors (not diverges from)
existing SDDRA patterns (EXPAND, 3-way registry, marketplace,
DONE-PROOF). No update, new skill, deprecation, or canonical
selection is required.

References retained:
  - security-hardening-events.md (this record, section 7) — L1
    reference for future generated-runtime security spec; requires
    separate DEC before any SDDRA spec change.

State: +
